    "long_instructions": "## Spot Checking the Data\r\n\r\nWe have a list of supplies, but the data is messy. Some items are missing information. Before we build a full display, we need to \"spot check\" specific items to see what the data looks like.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1.  **Retrieve Data:** In line 28,use the `getItemByIndex(1)` function to retrieve the microscope object and save it to a variable (e.g., `const myItem = ...`).\r\n2.  **Update Display:** Update the `textContent` for the **Name**, **Category**, and **Location** spans using the properties from your `myItem` variable.\r\n3.  **Observe:** Run the code. What text appears on the screen for the **Location**?\r\n4.  **Test Another:** Change your code to retrieve **index: 3** instead. What happens to the **Name** field?\r\n5.  **Optional Extend:** Ask AI to help write the other retrieval functions `getItemById` and `getItemByName` and then replace your calls to `getItemByIndex` with these new functions."
